From: MiniHub Contributors
Subject: esp-matter: value-init EspOtaRequestorEntry (no memset)

GCC -Werror=class-memaccess rejects memset on EspOtaRequestorEntry
because it embeds chip::ScopedNodeId (non-trivial). Value-initialize
instead so Matter OTA Provider builds under -Werror=cpp.

Component: esp-matter (sibling checkout via ESP_MATTER_PATH)
File: components/esp_matter_ota_provider/src/esp_matter_ota_provider.cpp
Apply-Root: ../esp-matter

Apply: ./tools/apply_component_patches.sh
---
--- a/components/esp_matter_ota_provider/src/esp_matter_ota_provider.cpp
+++ b/components/esp_matter_ota_provider/src/esp_matter_ota_provider.cpp
@@ -339,7 +339,8 @@ esp_err_t EspOtaProvider::CreateOtaRequestorEntry(const chip::ScopedNodeId &node
         if (!entry) {
             return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM;
         }
-        memset(entry, 0, sizeof(EspOtaRequestorEntry));
+        /* MiniHub: value-init EspOtaRequestorEntry (no memset on non-trivial type) */
+        *entry = EspOtaRequestorEntry{};
         entry->mNodeId = nodeId;
         entry->mOtaAllowed = mOtaAllowedDefault;
         entry->mNext = mOtaRequestorList;
